Description: Differential expression analysis is commonly used to study
    diverse biological datasets. The reproducibility-optimized test
    statistic (ROTS) (Elo et al., 2008, <doi:10.1109/tcbb.2007.1078>)
    uses a modified t-statistic to prioritise features that differ
    between two or more groups. However, the ROTS Bioconductor
    implementation (Suomi et al., 2017, <doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1005562>)
    did not accommodate technical or biological covariates. LimROTS
    (Anwar et al., 2025, <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btaf570>)
    addressed this limitation by combining a reproducibility-optimized
    test statistic with the limma empirical Bayes approach
    (Ritchie et al., 2015, <doi:10.1093/nar/gkv007>).
    This enables the analysis of more complex experimental designs
    and the incorporation of covariates.
